  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0404' consists of five tables: Employee, Supplier, Product, Employee_Sales, and Inventory.\nThe Employee table represents the employees of the organization. It has columns for Contact_Number, Employee_ID, Password, Position, and Username. The Employee_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Supplier table holds information about the suppliers. It includes Supplier_ID, Supplier_Name, Supplier_Number, and Supplier_Phone. The Supplier_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Product table contains information about the products. It includes Product_ID, Product_Name, Product_Number, Purchase_Price, Sales_Price, Stock_Quantity, and Supplier_ID. The Product_ID is the primary key and Supplier_ID is a foreign key referencing the Supplier table.\nThe Employee_Sales table records sales data. It includes Employee_ID, Product_ID, Sales_Date, Sales_Price, and Sales_Quantity. Employee_ID and Product_ID are the primary key of this table, and both are foreign keys referencing the Employee and Product tables respectively.\nLastly, the Inventory table keeps track of the inventory. It includes Inventory_ID, Product_ID, Sales_Price, and Stock_Quantity. The Product_ID is the foreign key referencing the Product table. The Inventory_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThis schema ensures entity integrity by having primary and foreign keys, and it also maintains referential integrity by ensuring that the foreign keys in the tables reference the primary keys of the related tables.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\nThe following describes a Product Sales Management System. The system’s main features might include:\n1.Employee Management: Includes managing employee usernames, passwords, positions, and contact information.\n2.Product Management: Includes managing product names, IDs, purchase prices, sales prices, and stock quantities.\n3.Supplier Management: Includes managing supplier names, IDs, and phone numbers. Suppliers can provide multiple products.\n4.Sales Management: Includes managing the sales records of product names, IDs, quantities, prices, and sales dates. Each employee can sell multiple products.\n5.Inventory Management: Includes managing product stock quantities and sales prices. Each product has a unique inventory record.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0404.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0404\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supplier` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `supplier_phone` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `purchase_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supplier_id`) REFERENCES `supplier` (`supplier_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_sales` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `sales_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_sales_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_sales_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inventory` (\n  `inventory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inventory_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
